Step 4: Multi-Account & Multi-Region Setup (us-east-1, us-east-2)
To collect metrics across AWS accounts and regions, use CloudWatch Cross-Account Observability.
4a. Designate a Central Monitoring Account
Pick one AWS account as the monitoring account (e.g., your ops/tooling account).
4b. In Each Source Account — Enable Sharing
Go to CloudWatch → Settings → Share data and:

Share with your central monitoring account ID
Select Metrics as the resource type
Scope to namespace: Ganz/Webkinz

Or via CLI on each source account:
bashaws oam create-link \
  --label-template "$AccountName" \
  --resource-types AWS::CloudWatch::Metric \
  --sink-identifier arn:aws:oam:us-east-1:MONITORING_ACCOUNT_ID:sink/YOUR_SINK_ID
4c. In the Central Monitoring Account — Create the Sink
bash# Create the sink
aws oam create-sink --name WNXTCentralSink --region us-east-1

# Attach a policy to allow source accounts to link
aws oam put-sink-policy \
  --sink-identifier arn:aws:oam:us-east-1:MONITORING_ACCOUNT_ID:sink/YOUR_SINK_ID \
  --policy '{
    "Version": "2012-10-17",
    "Statement": [{
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {
        "AWS": [
          "arn:aws:iam::SOURCE_ACCOUNT_1:root",
          "arn:aws:iam::SOURCE_ACCOUNT_2:root"
        ]
      },
      "Action": ["oam:CreateLink", "oam:UpdateLink"],
      "Resource": "*",
      "Condition": {
        "ForAllValues:StringEquals": {
          "oam:ResourceTypes": ["AWS::CloudWatch::Metric"]
        }
      }
    }]
  }'
4d. Repeat for us-east-2
Run the same sink setup in us-east-2 region of the central monitoring account, and link source accounts to both regional sinks.

Step 5: Create CloudWatch Alarms for Auto Scaling
In the central (or source) account, create alarms on the custom metric:
bashaws cloudwatch put-metric-alarm \
  --alarm-name "WNXT-HighCPU-ScaleOut" \
  --namespace "Ganz/Webkinz" \
  --metric-name "CPUUtilization" \
  --dimensions Name=AutoScalingGroupName,Value=WebkinzASG \
  --statistic Average \
  --period 60 \
  --threshold 70 \
  --comparison-operator GreaterThanOrEqualToThreshold \
  --evaluation-periods 2 \
  --alarm-actions arn:aws:autoscaling:us-east-1:ACCOUNT_ID:scalingPolicy:POLICY_ID

Step 6: Auto Scaling Group — Attach Scaling Policies
bash# Scale-Out Policy
aws autoscaling put-scaling-policy \
  --auto-scaling-group-name WebkinzASG \
  --policy-name WNXT-ScaleOut \
  --policy-type TargetTrackingScaling \
  --target-tracking-configuration '{
    "CustomizedMetricSpecification": {
      "MetricName": "CPUUtilization",
      "Namespace": "Ganz/Webkinz",
      "Dimensions": [{"Name": "AutoScalingGroupName", "Value": "WebkinzASG"}],
      "Statistic": "Average",
      "Unit": "Percent"
    },
    "TargetValue": 70.0
  }'

